<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="71915" href="schedule/2019/fall/STAT/578/71915.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2019" href="schedule/2019.xml">2019</calendarYear><term id="120198" href="schedule/2019/fall.xml">Fall 2019</term><subject id="STAT" href="schedule/2019/fall/STAT.xml">Statistics</subject><course id="578" href="schedule/2019/fall/STAT/578.xml">Topics in Statistics</course></parents><sectionNumber>GF </sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Sequential Detection</sectionTitle><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>The focus of this course will be on testing hypotheses and detecting changes when the data are collected in real time and the goal is to make an accurate decision as quickly as possible. Problems of design (controlled sensing) will also be considered, where one needs to specify a sampling mechanism in addition to a stopping rule and a decision rule.</sectionText><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2019-08-26Z</startDate><endDate>2019-12-11Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LCD">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>12:30 PM</start><end>01:50 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>TR     </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>136</roomNumber><buildingName>Loomis Laboratory</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Fellouris" firstName="G">Fellouris, G</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>